  "hints": [
    "Try to color the graph with two colors so neighbors always differ.",
    "BFS or DFS from every uncolored node, giving each neighbor the opposite color. A clash means it's not bipartite.",
    "color = [None]*n\nfor start in range(n):\n    if color[start] is None:\n        color[start] = 0; queue = [start]\n        while queue:\n            u = pop\n            for v in graph[u]:\n                if color[v] is None: color[v] = 1 - color[u]; push v\n                elif color[v] == color[u]: return false\nreturn true",
    "O(n + e). Starting a search from every uncolored node handles disconnected graphs."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(n + e)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
